                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "DAatS",
                          "name": "As implied, evaluating scale as an (x, y",
                          "context": "p",
                          "fill": "#fbf4ea",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                          "width": 307.63,
                          "height": 157.72,
                          "content": "As implied, evaluating scale as an (x, y, z) function empowers you to calculate spatial decay based exclusively on local position. You can instantly engineer complex tapers, rounded organic falloffs, or gracefully staggered architectural elements without stepping outside a single generative routine.",
